ASSUMPTION CHALLENGE
  Challenged assumption: the first Lean formalization should target the real
  LRC inequality or the full two-far rational kernel.  The more fundamental
  object is the finite currency-preservation quotient

    (r,t) -> {C(t-h)-C(t) : 0<=h<=min(r,t)}.

  This preserves the proof predicate "can this depth spend boundary margin?"
  and destroys actual phase probabilities, which are deliberately deferred to
  the later analytic estimates.
